## Context

Reported from padme, 2026-10-30, six landings in one interactive Claude Code
session (padme PRs #175, #177, #179, #180, #181, #182). Each `raid_land.py` run
printed at step 5a:

    attribution: invalid: line 3: fact order requires kind, pr, writer before reviewers (PR body: missing)

The review notes held gaze `reviewer:` lines but no `writer:` entry: only raid
and hunt record one (ticket 1307), and an interactive session that runs gaze,
verify-gate and merge by hand never does. `attribution_record.py --render-pr`
then refuses the block (`scripts/attribution_record.py:94`), the PR body keeps
no attribution, and roar's `--capture-unit` refuses too until a writer line is
added by hand (`--record-writer`, which itself demands step, route and
independence fields). The warning never blocks, so it is easy to ignore on
every landing.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] A landing from an interactive session either records the writer itself
      (merge skill or `raid_land.py`, from the session's runtime and model) or
      renders the reviewer lines without one, but does not print `invalid` for
      the ordinary case
- [ ] Roar's `--capture-unit` works on such a PR without a hand-typed writer line
- [ ] Test: a review on notes with gaze answers and no writer entry lands and
      captures with no `invalid` warning
- [ ] Widened (tracker 1382, memo `conception/2026-10-31-monitoring-redesign.md`
      § 4.1): when a fact is missing or malformed (duplicate finding at one
      anchor, a second writer line for a fix step, a ticket-only PR with no
      review), `--capture-unit` and the landing render what they can and print
      one `not derivable: <fact>` warning instead of refusing; test per case
- [ ] No path in landing or roar exits non-zero because of attribution alone

## Raid 8ad75a plan annotation (2026-10-31, lead)

Phases 2-3 compressed (one Imagine+Plan seat, sonnet; Blind-Spot+feasibility seat, opus): memo reviewed by four gaze rounds incl. cross-family. Feasibility: WARN (resolved below). Plan text: /tmp/raid-8ad75a/plan-1380.md (host padme).

Path: `salvage(text)` wrapper around the unchanged strict `parse_record`; `ensure_writer` records `writer: step=execute · ... · route=landing` when the review has none (never overwrites a raid/hunt writer); landing and capture print one `attribution: not derivable: <fact>` line per lost fact.
Lead rulings:
- Exit 5 keeps full scope: merge step 0 (`claims.md:45`, `--from-notes`), `raid_land`, `--render-pr`, `--capture-unit`, and roar runbook paths `--capture-pr` / `--seats-pr` never exit non-zero on attribution alone. A pure precondition (unit not merged) and an infrastructure failure (`memory-capture.sh`) may still exit 1.
- Session model/runtime default from `IDH_SESSION_MODEL` / `IDH_SESSION_RUNTIME` (existing convention, `gaze_close.py:346`, `seat_clock.py:423`), flag overrides.
- Fix-step case: build the fixture from the real failure text (journal entry of PR 2060), not a synthetic second execute writer that `notes_record` would collapse.
- Update `tests/test_raid_land.py:382` (`attribution: invalid` -> `not derivable`) and `tests/test_attribution_capture_pr.py:101`.
